gpu bridge: what the GPU drew goes into RAM before a state is taken

Under TCG the GL renderer writes a surface into the console's RAM only when
the processor reads it. A state is the machine's memory and nothing of the
driver's, and a load throws the GL objects away and rebuilds them from that
memory - so every surface drawn and not yet read was lost with the load: the
buffer about to be flipped, a render target a later pass samples, the half
of a frame already drawn. On a GTX 1060 the first frame after a load showed
the previous frame's picture in one game and five frames of leftovers and
black in another (chimera#190).

Upstream writes them out before its own savestates (nv2a_vm_state_change,
RUN_STATE_SAVE_VM). A sandbox snapshot runs no such hook, so
nv2a_chimera_flush_surfaces does the same on request, and the driver calls it
when the engine says a state is about to be taken (StateSaving).

diff --git a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/display.c b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/display.c
--- a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/display.c
+++ b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/display.c
@@ -474,3 +474,26 @@
     *out_h = h;
     return 1;
 }
+
+/* CHIMERA: what the GPU drew, into the machine. Under TCG a surface is written
+ * into the console's RAM only when the processor reads it; until then RAM
+ * holds whatever was there before and the picture is in the driver. A state is
+ * the machine's memory and nothing of the driver's, so one taken as things
+ * stand has the RAM of a console whose screen is elsewhere - and a load, which
+ * throws the GL objects away and rebuilds them from that RAM, loses every
+ * surface drawn and not yet read: the buffer about to be flipped, a render
+ * target a later pass samples, the half of a frame already drawn. Upstream
+ * does this before its own savestates (nv2a_vm_state_change, RUN_STATE_SAVE_VM);
+ * a sandbox snapshot runs no such hook, so the driver calls it from the
+ * engine's "a state is about to be taken" (StateSaving, chimera#190).
+ * The machine is stopped at a frame boundary; pre_savevm_wait services the
+ * request on this thread (pfifo_service_pending), as the display read does. */
+void nv2a_chimera_flush_surfaces(void)
+{
+    NV2AState *d = g_nv2a;
+    if (d == NULL || d->pgraph.gl_renderer_state == NULL) {
+        return;
+    }
+    pgraph_pre_savevm_trigger(d);
+    pgraph_pre_savevm_wait(d);
+}
diff --git a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.h b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.h
--- a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.h
+++ b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/gl/renderer.h
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@
 /* CHIMERA: the presented frame, read back for the driver's video export */
 int nv2a_chimera_read_display(uint8_t *out, int cap_w, int cap_h,
                               int *out_w, int *out_h);
+/* CHIMERA: the surfaces the GPU drew, written into RAM before a state is taken */
+void nv2a_chimera_flush_surfaces(void);
 #include "constants.h"
 
 typedef struct SurfaceBinding {
